<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jacobo Árbenz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1913–1971</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jacobo Árbenz was a Guatemalan army officer and politician who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a> from 1951 to 1954. A leader of the revolution of 1944, he carried out a land reform that expropriated uncultivated land of large estates, including that of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-fruit-company">United Fruit Company</a>. Accused of communist sympathies, he was overthrown in 1954 by a coup organised by the American CIA, and died in exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jacobo-arbenz.jpg" alt="Jacobo Árbenz" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gobierno de Guatemala · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Retrato_de_Presidente_Jacobo_%C3%81rbenz.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
